@@ -30,6 +31,7 @@ Statuses: `open`, `doing`, `done`. Errors are `{"error":"..."}`.
 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task requires manager of its current project, and write access to the destination (contributor or manager there). The move keeps the task's ID, title, status and assignee. The assignee must also be a contributor or manager of the destination, otherwise the move is rejected with 400 and nothing changes. Moving to the same project → 400. A missing `toProjectId` → 400. Destination not readable → 404; destination viewer-only → 403; destination archived → 409.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
